# Tests of the `handles` module; generated from tools/handles.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

# Tests keep a region's header in the last 4 KiB of machine.state (from byte 61440), which the runtime's own state
# never reaches.
handleTest is test
handleTest purpose "Handles are numbered in order, name their objects and kinds, are listed by their region, and are closed when it is released"
handleTest verifies newHandle numbersHandles
handleTest verifies kindOf knowsKind
handleTest verifies objectOf givesObject
handleTest verifies drop closesHandle
handleTest verifies dropRegion dropsOwned
handleTest typeParameter none
handleTest input none
handleTest output none
handleTest outputOwnedBy none
handleTest raises none
handleTest effect use machine.memory
handleTest effect use system.calls
handleTest uses memoryAccess
handleTest uses systemCalls
handleTest memoryHeap false
handleTest async false
handleTest maxRecursion none
handleTest label begin loopKind none
handleTest label begin within none
handleTest let regionAt Int64 61440 immutable
handleTest let zeroByte Byte 0 immutable
handleTest let sixtyFour Int64 64 immutable
handleTest let fortyEight Int64 48 immutable
handleTest let tableBytes Int64 88 immutable
handleTest let zero Int64 0 immutable
handleTest let minusOne Int64 -1 immutable
handleTest let one Int64 1 immutable
handleTest let fiftySix Int64 56 immutable
